# Signalpost — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in only what you intend to use:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored and must never be committed. Every value below is a
# PLACEHOLDER. Nothing here is a real credential.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The submitted run path reads NO environment variables at all.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `uv run main.py -i data/corpus/corpus.jsonl -o out/run.jsonl` uses only free,
# official, unauthenticated Norwegian registry APIs and direct company websites.
# Third-party spend is $0.00 and there is no key to configure or leak. You can verify
# this claim directly:
#
#     grep -rn "environ\|getenv" src/signalpost/     # returns nothing
#
# The variables below are read by optional side scripts under `scripts/`, which are
# NOT part of the submitted run path and are not invoked by `main.py`. They exist so a
# paid discovery experiment can be run deliberately, by a human, with a key that human
# supplied. Leaving every variable unset is the supported configuration.

# --- scripts/run_brave_discovery.py -------------------------------------------
# Brave Search API — https://brave.com/search/api/
# Chargeable. Used only to PROPOSE website candidates for companies where the registry
# lists no site. Per the organiser's source policy, "search results generate
# candidates; they are not claim evidence": a search hit is never published as a fact
# and never bypasses the identity gate in src/signalpost/identity.py.
#
# Read via `--api-key-env`, which defaults to this name:
# BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY=your-brave-subscription-token
